      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "The protein family described here is characterized by its ability to bind calcium, which suggests a role in cellular signaling events. Members of the family are found across various species, including humans, mice, rabbits, bovines, and crustaceans. While some members are hypothesized to function as regulatory proteins rather than as calcium buffers or transport proteins, the exact mechanisms by which they influence signaling pathways remain to be fully elucidated. The potential regulatory function implies that these proteins may interact with other cellular components to modulate processes that are sensitive to calcium levels, which is a common second messenger in many signaling cascades.",
